# what a handler edge hands over is read in a landing pad, and all the pads of a handler stand in a row just ahead of it, far behind the blocks that lead to them.
# Between the last of those blocks and its pad such a value lies unread, so its place is another's there: values that follow each other take turns in two places, however long the try is.
# Without that each has a word of its own, and every resumption clears that word: the frames here were 128 and 112 bytes, and a large async function had 36,368 bytes, 33,376 of them cleared each time.
# async function waits(make, awaited) { let last = make(make); try { make(last); last = make(make); .. eight times ..; return await awaited; } catch { return make(last); } }
# function calls(make, other) { the same, with make(other) in the place of the await }
# The last value of `waits` is held by the await, and has its gap like the others. checkAllocation() forgets a spill on an edge into its gap, and finds every pad served.
# REQUIRES: not-windows
# RUN: allocate f1:CoroutineBody f2:Body mechanisms=none
# CHECK-LABEL: unit f1:CoroutineBody
# CHECK-COUNT-9: 64 bits, gap
# CHECK-NOT: gap
# CHECK-LABEL: unit f2:Body
# CHECK-COUNT-9: 64 bits, gap
# CHECK-NOT: gap
# REQUIRES(PLACES): x86_64 not-windows
# RUN(PLACES): frame f1:CoroutineBody f2:Body mechanisms=none
# PLACES-LABEL: unit f1:CoroutineBody
# PLACES: bytesDeadAtSuspensions = 40
# PLACES: s3 at -[[one]]
# PLACES-NEXT: s4 at -[[other]]
# PLACES-NEXT: s5 at -[[one]]
# PLACES-NEXT: s6 at -[[other]]
# PLACES-NEXT: s7 at -[[one]]
# PLACES-NEXT: s8 at -[[other]]
# PLACES-NEXT: s9 at -[[one]]
# PLACES-NEXT: s10 at -[[other]]
# PLACES-LABEL: unit f2:Body
# PLACES: size = 48
# PLACES: s2 at -[[third]]
# PLACES-NEXT: s3 at -[[fourth]]
# PLACES-NEXT: s4 at -[[third]]
# PLACES-NEXT: s5 at -[[fourth]]
# PLACES-NEXT: s6 at -[[third]]
# PLACES-NEXT: s7 at -[[fourth]]
# PLACES-NEXT: s8 at -[[third]]
# PLACES-NEXT: s9 at -[[fourth]]
# PLACES-NEXT: s10 at -[[third]]
# REQUIRES(PLACESARM): arm64
# RUN(PLACESARM): frame f1:CoroutineBody f2:Body mechanisms=none
# PLACESARM-LABEL: unit f1:CoroutineBody
# PLACESARM: s2 at -[[one]]
# PLACESARM-NEXT: s3 at -[[other]]
# PLACESARM-NEXT: s4 at -[[one]]
# PLACESARM-NEXT: s5 at -[[other]]
# PLACESARM-NEXT: s6 at -[[one]]
# PLACESARM-NEXT: s7 at -[[other]]
# PLACESARM-NEXT: s8 at -[[one]]
# PLACESARM-NEXT: s9 at -[[other]]
# PLACESARM-LABEL: unit f2:Body
# PLACESARM: s1 at -[[third]]
# PLACESARM-NEXT: s2 at -[[fourth]]
# PLACESARM-NEXT: s3 at -[[third]]
# PLACESARM-NEXT: s4 at -[[fourth]]
# PLACESARM-NEXT: s5 at -[[third]]
# PLACESARM-NEXT: s6 at -[[fourth]]
# PLACESARM-NEXT: s7 at -[[third]]
# PLACESARM-NEXT: s8 at -[[fourth]]
# PLACESARM-NEXT: s9 at -[[third]]
# REQUIRES(FRAME): x86_64 not-windows
# RUN(FRAME): frame f1:CoroutineBody mechanisms=none
# FRAME: size = 80
# REQUIRES(ARM): arm64
# RUN(ARM): frame f1:CoroutineBody mechanisms=none
# ARM: size = 80

